From c7c5b1ef747adab717b97d60026cb22e37f9c25e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 05:55:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] test(app): pin the shank cause of the flute_reach rapid
 findings

The heavy test a_ten_mm_flute_names_its_cause_before_the_rapid_findings
counted 3 rapid findings. The ring plan of #3790 (6c164521f) made it 12,
and #3818 made it 9. Each finding is a vertical lift or drop at the two
corners where the shank of the 10 mm flute stands in the part wall. They
are real contacts and they hold the post. The same path with a 25 mm
flute has no contact finding.

The test now asserts the cause: each RapidInPart is a lift or a drop
whose low end puts the shank under the part top, and there is no gouge
and no RapidInStock. The 25 mm flute test asserts that a tool that
reaches meets nothing.

Fixes #3811

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
